---
import DetailLayout from "../../layouts/DetailLayout.astro";
---

<DetailLayout
  title="Tiger Leaping Gorge"
  description="Tiger Leaping Gorge, Shangri-La Yunnan: world-class 2-day gorge trek with guesthouses. Transport from Shangri-La and Lijiang, best season, safety tips."
  category="Attraction"
  image="tiger-leaping-gorge.webp"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "TouristAttraction",
    "name": "Tiger Leaping Gorge",
    "description": "One of the deepest river gorges in the world near Shangri-La Yunnan. Legendary 2-day high trail hike with guesthouses along the route and dramatic views of Jade Dragon Snow Mountain.",
    "publicAccess": true
  }}
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Tiger Leaping Gorge</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">One of the deepest gorges on Earth. A legendary 2-day high trail trek between Jade Dragon Snow Mountain and Haba Snow Mountain. Guesthouses, dramatic views, and the roaring Jinsha River 3,900 meters below.</p>

  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Altitude</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">1,800&ndash;2,670 m</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Time Needed</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">1&ndash;2 days</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Best Season</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Apr&ndash;Jun, Sep&ndash;Oct</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Ticket</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">65 RMB</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Tiger Leaping Gorge (u864eu8df3u5ce1) is one of the deepest river gorges in the world, where the Jinsha River (upper Yangtze) carves a chasm between the 5,596-meter Jade Dragon Snow Mountain and the 5,396-meter Haba Snow Mountain. At its deepest point, the canyon drops 3,900 meters from peak to river &mdash; deeper than the Grand Canyon.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">According to legend, a tiger being hunted jumped across the narrowest point of the gorge (about 25 meters) to escape, giving the gorge its name. Today that spot, known as Tiger Leaping Rock, is the most dramatic section of the trail.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The gorge offers two distinct experiences. The <strong>High Trail</strong> (upper route) is a world-class 2-day trek following the cliffside at 2,400&ndash;2,670 meters, with guesthouses spaced every few hours of walking. The <strong>lower road</strong> is accessible by car and bus, visiting the paved tourist viewing platforms at the upper gorge section. Serious trekkers do the high trail; photographers and short-visit travelers enjoy the lower gorge.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">The High Trail: 2-Day Trek Itinerary</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Day 1: Qiaotou &rarr; Naxi Guesthouse (5&ndash;6 hours, 12 km)</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Start at Qiaotou village (1,800m). The first 2 hours are the steepest: the infamous "28 Bends" switchback climb gains 500 meters of elevation. Push through &mdash; once past the bends, the trail levels into a spectacular high traverse with Jade Dragon Snow Mountain filling the entire sky to your left. Lunch at the Tea Horse Guesthouse. End the day at Naxi Family Guesthouse or Halfway Guesthouse (both around 2,500m). Halfway has a legendary viewing platform for sunset.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Day 2: Guesthouse &rarr; Tina's &rarr; River (4&ndash;5 hours, 10 km)</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Morning walk along a gentler high trail with waterfalls and bamboo groves. After 2 hours, descend to Tina's Guesthouse on the lower road. From here, an optional steep 1-hour descent takes you to the Tiger Leaping Rock at river level &mdash; the most dramatic viewpoint in the gorge. Climb back up (1&ndash;1.5 hours) or take a hired horse (100&ndash;150 RMB). Buses back to Lijiang or Shangri-La depart from Tina's at 3:30 PM.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">How to Get There</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">From Shangri-La</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Drive 2&ndash;2.5 hours to Qiaotou village. A private car costs <strong>400&ndash;600 RMB</strong> one way. The driver can drop you at the trailhead and arrange pickup at Tina's Guesthouse the next day.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">From Lijiang</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Lijiang is the more common starting point (2 hours to Qiaotou). Public buses from Lijiang Bus Station depart at 8:00 AM and 9:30 AM, fare <strong>40&ndash;50 RMB</strong>. The bus will drop you at Qiaotou trailhead if you tell the driver.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Where to Stay &amp; Eat on the Trail</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Guesthouses on the high trail are simple but comfortable: dorm beds <strong>40&ndash;60 RMB</strong>, private rooms <strong>120&ndash;200 RMB</strong>. All serve meals &mdash; fried rice, noodle soups, Naxi grilled fish, stir-fried vegetables (20&ndash;40 RMB per dish). Hot showers are available but can be unreliable; the best guesthouses (Halfway, Naxi Family) have solar-heated water. No need to carry a tent or stove.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Safety &amp; Practical Tips</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span><strong>No guide needed.</strong> The high trail is well-marked with painted arrows and signs. Guesthouses are spaced 2&ndash;3 hours apart.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span><strong>Avoid rainy season</strong> (July&ndash;August). The trail becomes slippery and landslides can block access. Check conditions with your guesthouse.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Pack light: one change of clothes, rain jacket, sunscreen, 2 liters of water, snacks. Leave your main luggage at your hotel in Lijiang or Shangri-La.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>The trail elevation (2,400m) is lower than Shangri-La city. Altitude sickness is rarely an issue.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-700">Nearby &raquo;</p>
    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a href="/attractions/meili-snow-mountain" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Meili Snow Mountain</a>
      <a href="/attractions/balagezong-canyon" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Balagezong Canyon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DetailLayout>